     Default: 0.2 (200 ms).
 
+``--audio-crossfade-buffer=<seconds>``
+    Reserve additional decoded PCM lookahead for ``crossfade-loadfile``. Accepts
+    0 to 30 seconds, limited to 64 MiB according to the output format. Zero is
+    the default and leaves ordinary buffering and startup behavior unchanged.
+    This does not enable cross-fading or schedule playlist transitions by itself.
+
+    Set this before loading a file. Enabling it can require more initial decoding,
+    network buffering and memory, and buffered filter/speed changes may react
+    later. A cross-fade can only retain audio that has actually been decoded;
+    inspect ``audio-crossfade/available`` when deciding when to request one.
+    Changing the option during playback reconfigures the audio output.
+
 ``--audio-stream-silence=<yes|no>``
     Cash-grab consumer audio hardware (such as A/V receivers) often ignore
     initial audio sent over HDMI. This can happen every time audio over HDMI
